"""Routes by Jev's judgment and moves one acting memory onto a decision program.

learn keeps the stored memories (or learns the kinds on a first run), lifts acting memories off reasoning
"none", has the writer build a router that asks Jev which memory fits, raises the level of any memory the
model still gets wrong, and then has the writer write a decision program for the busiest acting memory.
The program is stored only if practice shows no wrong action and a better reward than the model earns.
"""

KINDS_PROMPT = """{contract}

Below are runs where the assistant, a language model, handled requests for
this job: each request, every tool call with its result, and the verdict.
Some requests are worded oddly, some should not be acted on at all, and
some runs went wrong.

List the kinds of request these runs show, and for each write what the
assistant should know the next time it meets one: how ids are really
written in the tools, which tools to call and in what order, and the
mistakes to avoid. Use as few kinds as cover the runs.

Reply with only a JSON list. Each item has the keys "name" (short, in
snake_case), "description" (which requests belong to this kind, and which
similar ones don't), "guidance" (what the assistant should know), and
"acts" (true if a request of this kind should end in an action, false if
it should only be answered or passed on).

{episodes}"""

ROUTER_PROMPT = """{contract}

Write the routing program for this job: Python source defining
`async def decide(request, kit)`. It picks which stored memory serves a request.

The stored memories (kit.recall returns them as dicts with "name", "description",
"route" and "read_only"):
{memories}

What the program must do:
- call `await kit.recall(request, 6)` to get the candidate memories;
- ask Jev (as the contract above describes) for a typed judgment of which
  candidate fits the request, showing Jev each candidate's name, its description
  and whether it can act. Tell Jev: a request that asks for work this job does
  must go to a memory that can act (read_only false); a request that only asks a
  question, asks about the past, asks for something to be changed or withheld
  rather than done, or is outside the job must go to a read_only memory;
- check that Jev's answer is one of the candidate names; if it is not, or Jev
  fails, serve the first recalled candidate; if nothing was recalled, hand off
  as the contract says;
- return a dict whose only key is "serve" and whose value is the chosen name.

Rules: never decide what the request means by searching it for words or
patterns; that judgment is Jev's alone. No imports, no names starting with an
underscore, no bare except (use `except Exception`), no str.format. The only
builtins are Exception, KeyError, TypeError, ValueError, abs, all, any, bool,
dict, divmod, enumerate, filter, float, int, isinstance, len, list, map, max,
min, range, reversed, round, set, sorted, str, sum, tuple, zip.

Some requests, for a sense of wording only (unseen requests are worded differently):
{samples}
{report}
Reply with only the Python source."""

PROGRAM_PROMPT = """{contract}

Write a decision program for one kind of request in this job: Python source
defining `async def decide(request, kit)` that serves the request fully with no
language model, exactly as the contract above describes.

The kind of request it serves:
name: {name}
description: {description}
what the assistant learned about it:
{body}

Runs where a language model handled requests of this job (each tool call with
its arguments and result, and the checker's verdict). Copy what the successful
runs did: the same tools, the same order, ids written the same way, the same
final action.
{episodes}

Requests of this kind, for a sense of wording only (unseen requests are worded
differently and may ask for variants, such as a different count, window or limit):
{samples}

How to write it:
- everything about what the request asks for (who, what, how long, how many,
  which days, earliest start, latest end, and so on) comes from asking Jev for
  typed judgments, one small clear question at a time, never from searching the
  request for words or patterns;
- everything exact (looking up ids, reading tool results, comparing times,
  searching for a choice that meets every constraint) is done in code, with
  times converted to numbers before comparing;
- check Jev's answers against what the tools return (for example that every
  named person or item was found). If an answer is missing or inconsistent, a
  tool fails, or no choice meets every constraint, hand off as the contract
  says instead of acting. A wrong action is far worse than a hand-off;
- cover the variants the description mentions (for example more than one item
  to create, each meeting its own constraints) if code can do them exactly.

Rules: no imports, no names starting with an underscore, no bare except (use
`except Exception`), no str.format. The only builtins are Exception, KeyError,
TypeError, ValueError, abs, all, any, bool, dict, divmod, enumerate, filter,
float, int, isinstance, len, list, map, max, min, range, reversed, round, set,
sorted, str, sum, tuple, zip.
{report}
Reply with only the Python source."""

ROUTER = """async def decide(request, kit):
    found = await kit.recall(request, k=1)
    if len(found) == 0:
        return {"handoff": "nothing learned applies"}
    return {"serve": found[0]["name"]}
"""

ACT_LEVEL = "low"
LEVELS = ["none", "low", "medium", "high"]
MAX_IDS = 16


def code_of(reply):
    text = str(reply)
    if "```" in text:
        best = ""
        for chunk in text.split("```"):
            if "async def decide" in chunk and len(chunk) > len(best):
                best = chunk
        if best != "":
            text = best
            for tag in ["python3", "python", "py"]:
                if text.startswith(tag):
                    text = text[len(tag):]
                    break
    return text.strip() + "\n"


async def run(lab, source, ids):
    out = []
    for tid in ids:
        try:
            got = await lab.practice(source, tid)
            out.append((tid, float(got[0]), str(got[1]), got[2]))
        except Exception as error:
            out.append((tid, 0.0, "error: " + str(error), None))
    return out


def total(results):
    return sum(r[1] for r in results)


def no_zero(results):
    return all(r[1] > 0 for r in results)


def describe(lab, results):
    lines = []
    for r in results:
        lines.append("- request: " + str(lab.request(r[0])) + "\n  reward " + str(r[1]) + ", served by "
                     + str(r[3]) + ": " + r[2])
    return "\n".join(lines)


def store(lab, memory):
    lab.remember(memory["name"], memory["description"], memory["body"], route=memory["route"],
                 read_only=bool(memory.get("read_only", False)))


async def learn(lab):
    # 1. the memories: the parent's, or the kinds seen in the runs
    memories = []
    if len(lab.memories) > 0:
        for memory in lab.memories:
            memories.append(dict(memory))
    else:
        shown = "\n\n".join(lab.render(e) for e in lab.episodes)
        reply = await lab.ask(lab.fill(KINDS_PROMPT, contract=lab.contract, episodes=shown))
        for kind in lab.parse(reply):
            memories.append({"name": kind["name"], "description": kind["description"], "body": kind["guidance"],
                             "route": "none", "read_only": not kind["acts"]})
    for memory in memories:
        if not memory.get("read_only", False) and memory.get("route") == "none":
            memory["route"] = ACT_LEVEL
        store(lab, memory)
    by_name = dict((m["name"], m) for m in memories)

    # the requests to try things on
    should = {}
    ids = []
    for test in lab.tests:
        should[test["id"]] = bool(test["should_act"])
        ids.append(test["id"])
    if len(ids) == 0:
        ids = list(lab.stream())
    ids = ids[:MAX_IDS]
    samples = "\n".join("- " + str(lab.request(t)) for t in ids[:10])
    listing = "\n".join("- " + m["name"] + " (read_only " + str(bool(m.get("read_only", False))) + "): "
                        + str(m["description"]) for m in memories)

    def misrouted(results):
        bad = []
        for r in results:
            served = by_name.get(r[3])
            if r[2].startswith("error") or served is None:
                bad.append(r)
            elif r[0] in should and should[r[0]] == bool(served.get("read_only", False)):
                bad.append(r)
        return bad

    # 2. a router that asks Jev
    router = ROUTER
    results = []
    try:
        reply = await lab.ask(lab.fill(ROUTER_PROMPT, contract=lab.contract, memories=listing, samples=samples,
                                       report=""))
        candidate = code_of(reply)
        results = await run(lab, candidate, ids)
        bad = misrouted(results)
        if len(bad) > 0:
            report = ("\nAn earlier attempt is below, with the requests it sent to the wrong kind of memory or "
                      "failed on. Fix it.\n" + candidate + "\n" + describe(lab, bad) + "\n")
            reply = await lab.ask(lab.fill(ROUTER_PROMPT, contract=lab.contract, memories=listing,
                                           samples=samples, report=report))
            second = code_of(reply)
            again = await run(lab, second, ids)
            if len(misrouted(again)) < len(bad) or total(again) > total(results):
                candidate = second
                results = again
        if len(results) > 0 and no_zero(results) and total(results) / len(results) >= 0.5:
            router = candidate
        else:
            results = await run(lab, ROUTER, ids)
    except Exception as error:
        lab.note("router writing failed: " + str(error))
        results = await run(lab, ROUTER, ids)

    # 3. raise the level of acting memories the model still gets wrong
    for step in range(2):
        failing = {}
        for r in results:
            served = by_name.get(r[3])
            if served is None or served.get("read_only", False) or served.get("route") == "program":
                continue
            if should.get(r[0], False) and r[1] < 0.6:
                failing.setdefault(r[3], []).append(r[0])
        if len(failing) == 0:
            break
        retry = []
        for name in failing:
            memory = by_name[name]
            level = memory.get("route")
            if level in LEVELS and LEVELS.index(level) < len(LEVELS) - 1:
                memory["route"] = LEVELS[LEVELS.index(level) + 1]
                store(lab, memory)
                retry = retry + failing[name]
        if len(retry) == 0:
            break
        fresh = dict((r[0], r) for r in await run(lab, router, retry))
        results = [fresh.get(r[0], r) for r in results]

    # 4. move one acting memory onto a decision program
    counts = {}
    for r in results:
        served = by_name.get(r[3])
        if served is None or served.get("read_only", False) or served.get("route") == "program":
            continue
        if should.get(r[0], r[1] >= 0.6):
            counts.setdefault(r[3], []).append(r[0])
    if len(counts) > 0:
        name = sorted(counts, key=lambda n: -len(counts[n]))[0]
        target = by_name[name]
        mine = counts[name]
        try:
            shown = "\n\n".join(lab.render(e) for e in lab.episodes)
            wording = "\n".join("- " + str(lab.request(t)) for t in mine)
            reply = await lab.ask(lab.fill(PROGRAM_PROMPT, contract=lab.contract, name=name,
                                           description=target["description"], body=target["body"],
                                           episodes=shown, samples=wording, report=""))
            program = code_of(reply)
            tried = await run(lab, program, mine)
            if any(r[1] < 1 for r in tried):
                report = ("\nAn earlier attempt is below with what happened on each request. Fix what went "
                          "wrong and keep what worked.\n" + program + "\n" + describe(lab, tried) + "\n")
                reply = await lab.ask(lab.fill(PROGRAM_PROMPT, contract=lab.contract, name=name,
                                               description=target["description"], body=target["body"],
                                               episodes=shown, samples=wording, report=report))
                second = code_of(reply)
                again = await run(lab, second, mine)
                if (no_zero(again) and not no_zero(tried)) or (no_zero(again) and total(again) > total(tried)):
                    program = second
                    tried = again
            if len(tried) > 0 and no_zero(tried) and total(tried) / len(tried) > 0.6:
                lab.remember(name, target["description"], program, route="program", read_only=False)
                lab.note("moved " + name + " to a program, mean reward " + str(total(tried) / len(tried)))
            else:
                lab.note("program for " + name + " not kept: " + describe(lab, tried))
        except Exception as error:
            lab.note("program writing failed: " + str(error))
    return router

